# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(a) You can simply use intuition and symmetry to say $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0$. To show explicitly:\n"
msgstr "(a) Puoi semplicemente usare l'intuizione e la simmetria per dire che $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0$. Per mostrarlo esplicitamente:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\langle0|+\\langle1|) Z \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}(\\langle0|Z|0\\rangle+\\langle0|Z|1\\rangle+\\langle1|Z|0\\rangle+\\langle1|Z|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}((1)\\langle0|0\\rangle+(-1)\\langle0|1\\rangle+(1)\\langle1|0\\rangle+(-1)\\langle1|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}(1+0+0+-1)\\\\\n"
"& = 0\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\langle0|+\\langle1|) Z \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}(\\langle0|Z|0\\rangle+\\langle0|Z|1\\rangle+\\langle1|Z|0\\rangle+\\langle1|Z|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}((1)\\langle0|0\\rangle+(-1)\\langle0|1\\rangle+(1)\\langle1|0\\rangle+(-1)\\langle1|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}(1+0+0+-1)\\\\\n"
"& = 0\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(b) The state could collapse to either $|0\\rangle$ or $|1\\rangle$ when measured, each with 50% chance. But of the 50% that collapse to the $|0\\rangle$ state, 1% of those (or 0.5% of all cases) will be mis-reported as $|1\\rangle$. Of the 50% that collapse to $|1\\rangle$, 10% (or 5% of all cases) will be mis-reported as $|0\\rangle$. This leaves us with:\n"
"* $|0\\rangle$ 54.5%\n"
"* $|1\\rangle$ 45.5%\n"
"Ignoring all other types of possible errors, we would obtain an estimate of\n"
msgstr ""
"(b) Lo stato potrebbe collassare su $|0\\rangle$ o su $|1\\rangle$ quando viene misurato, ciascuno con il 50% di probabilità. Ma del 50% che collassa sullo stato $|0\\rangle$, l'1% (ovvero lo 0,5% di tutti i casi) verrà riportato erroneamente come $|1\\rangle$. Del 50% che collassa su $|1\\rangle$, il 10% (ovvero il 5% di tutti i casi) verrà riportato erroneamente come $|0\\rangle$. Questo ci lascia con:\n"
"* $|0\\rangle$ 54,5%\n"
"* $|1\\rangle$ 45,5%\n"
"Ignorando tutti gli altri tipi di errori possibili, otterremmo una stima di\n"

